CLAUDE.md

# E7 conditioning raw arrays: 3.1 MB of dense correlation matrices, regenerable by
# re-running `python -m experiments.e7_interface_ablation --force` (~7 min). The scientific
# content (condition number, singular values, height-distance correlation block, interface
# spread stats) is committed in interface_ablation_conditioning.json. Excluded to respect
# the repo-wide 1000 KB large-file policy (.pre-commit-config.yaml check-added-large-files).
experiments/results/interface_ablation_conditioning.npz

# E1's per-point spatial-error CSV (experiments/e1_refractive_comparison.py) is
# ~11MB -- 8 depths x 2 models x every adjacent-corner-pair in a dense N_GRID=7
# sweep -- which exceeds this repo's check-added-large-files --maxkb=1000 gate.
# It has no committed baseline (D-20) and is not compared by --check; it is
# fully deterministic and reproduced on demand via
# `python -m experiments.e1_refractive_comparison --out experiments/results --force`.
experiments/results/exp2_spatial_errors.csv

# Seed-sweep working directories. These are noise-floor MEASUREMENTS used to
# decide whether a movement is real (D-19.3-17), not manuscript artifacts: each
# run writes a full experiment output tree per seed, which is large and is
# summarised into MANUSCRIPT-FINDINGS.md rather than committed.
seed_sweep_19_2/
seed_sweep_19_3/

# Dry-run state from experiments/rerun_19_5.sh -- control-flow rehearsal
# only, never a record of a real run (see that script's STATE_FILE block).
experiments/rerun_19_5_state.dryrun.tsv

# Pre-launch gate log (phase 19.5) -- rerunnable, not an artifact
experiments/prelaunch_gate_19_5.log

# The production queue log IS a citable artifact -- it is the human-readable
# record of which seeds were requested (see the 19.4 band-sidecar todo, which
# cites rerun_19_4.log for exactly that). Un-ignore it against *.log above so
# plan 10 commits it without needing "git add -f".
!experiments/rerun_19_5.log
